ers at a pair of christchurch  mosques  she immediately promised action i can  tell you one thing right now  our gun laws will change and while she  joined her country in grieving the dead  she pushed through tough gun laws many  thought impossible  we will close our border to any  non-residents and citizens  she was as decisive in dealing with the  pandemic closing new zealand's borders  to foreigners  in february and after a strict lockdown  announced in june the country  had effectively wiped out covet 19. i  did a little dance  now the hard work begins for the leader  dubbed the anti-trump  mike turley global news toronto  saving or costing lives still ahead the  immunity issue  splitting scientists  in a pandemic herd immunity is the holy  grail the point at which enough people  are immune to protect those who are not  it can come from a protective vaccine  or after enough people get infected now  a controversial declaration by a group  of scientists suggests  almost all schools and businesses around  the world should reopen  to expedite immunity from covet 19.  other eminent researchers are aghast at  an idea  they say would cost more lives eric  sorenson reports  when president trump encourages crowds  to gather without requiring masks or  distancing  he is in effect promoting a strategy to  speed up transmission of the novel  coronavirus  to achieve herd immunity sooner it  happens people have it and it goes  get the kids back to school we got to  get the kids back to school  the approach would drop restrictions and  allow the virus to run through the  younger stronger population  while protecting the elderly and  vulnerable white house officials have  cited the barrington declaration  signed by dozens of doctors stating in  part those who are not vulnerable should  immediately be allowed to resume  life as normal this canadian doctor  co-signed the petition  i would like to see healthy young people  get back to work because they're very  low risk  uh of cop